Digital twins—virtual replicas of physical systems—are gaining traction in manufacturing. These technologies allow manufacturers to simulate processes and test changes in a virtual environment before implementation, reducing risks and costs.

- **Example**: General Motors utilizes digital twins to simulate vehicle assembly processes. This technology enables the company to optimize workflows and identify potential bottlenecks before making changes on the production floor.

